1
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:10,260
OK, Philip. This is your third cup of coffee.

2
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,520
We should get to work,

3
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:14,710
or we won't be finished by dinnertime.

4
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:16,290
I guess we must.

5
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:19,300
We must.

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:31,100
OK. The beginning of my famous Thanksgiving apple pie.

7
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:37,580
One apple. Two apples. Three apples. Four apples.

8
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:39,300
Come on, Philip!

9
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,510
Get busy with your famous apple pie.

10
00:00:41,510 --> 00:00:43,340
There's much more to be done.

11
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,370
Now, the ingredients.

12
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:45,820
What goes into my apple pie besides apples?

13
00:00:45,820 --> 00:01:02,250
Ah, yes. Flour, sugar, butter.

14
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:06,080
Butter, nice and cold and hard.

15
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:08,340
OK, here are the walnuts.

16
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:09,850
Last but not least,

17
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:15,030
the reason my apple pie is famous--cinnamon.

18
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:18,760
Cinnamon ...

19
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:20,640
Ellen, where's the cinnamon?

20
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:20,740
If there is any cinnamon,

21
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:33,400
it's in the cabinet with the salt and pepper.

22
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:39,790
Salt, pepper, dill weed, garlic powder, cinnamon. Ellen?

23
00:01:39,790 --> 00:01:41,300
Yes, Philip.

24
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:45,970
Is it possible that we forgot to buy cinnamon?

25
00:01:45,970 --> 00:01:51,570
Yes, it is possible that we forgot to buy cinnamon.

26
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:55,410
Well, how can I make my famous apple pie without cinnamon?

27
00:01:55,410 --> 00:01:56,830
Good morning.

28
00:01:56,830 --> 00:01:58,520
Oh, hi, Robbie. Good morning.

29
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:00,990
Good morning. Robbie.

30
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:02,250
Can you do me a favor?

31
00:02:02,250 --> 00:02:04,100
Sure, Dad. What?

32
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:07,610
Remember my apple pie on Thanksgiving?

33
00:02:07,610 --> 00:02:11,790
What do you love about it?

34
00:02:11,790 --> 00:02:12,830
The apples?

35
00:02:12,830 --> 00:02:15,010
No. The sssss...

36
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:16,360
Cinnamon.

37
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:20,760
Right. We don't have any cinnamon.

38
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:23,680
I'll go down to Henry's grocery. He's always open.

39
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,660
I'll get some for you.

40
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:27,560
That's my boy!

41
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,570
Oh, put your heavy jacket on, Robbie.

42
00:02:29,570 --> 00:02:34,030
It's cold outside.

43
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:36,460
Alexandra might call.

44
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:37,980
Tell her I'll call her right back.

45
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:39,680
OK.

46
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:44,840
Thanks, Son.

47
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:59,880
Uh, why does he always have to slam the door?

48
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:05,280
Hello.... Hello, Alexandra. How are you? ... Fine.

49
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:07,030
Robbie just went to the store.

50
00:03:07,030 --> 00:03:08,300
He'll be back soon.

51
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:10,130
He said he'll call you.

52
00:03:10,130 --> 00:03:15,840
... Oh, oh, I see.... Oh ... certainly. ...

53
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:18,640
Well, do you have the phone number there?

54
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:24,480
... Oh ... I see.... Please, I know he wants to talk to you.... ...

55
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,310
Thank you,

56
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:29,170
and happy Thanksgiving to you and your family, too.

57
00:03:29,170 --> 00:03:34,830
Try to come by later for dessert.... Bye.

58
00:03:34,830 --> 00:03:36,310
That was Alexandra.

59
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:37,800
She and the Molinas

60
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,180
are going to spend Thanksgiving with their cousins.

61
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:41,980
She doesn't have the phone number.

62
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:44,620
Oh, Robbie will be disappointed.

63
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:46,840
He'll be grouchy.

64
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:51,730
Maybe she'll call back. She promised.

65
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:59,450
Here's your cinnamon, Pop.

66
00:03:59,450 --> 00:04:05,170
It was a dollar and sixty cents.

67
00:04:05,170 --> 00:04:08,420
You forgot to ask me for the change.

68
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:18,040
Or did you forget to give it to me?

69
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:21,380
Thanks, Son.

70
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:23,200
Alexandra called.

71
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,340
I'll call her back.

72
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:25,990
She said she'll call you later.

73
00:04:25,990 --> 00:04:37,960
She's not at home.

74
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:39,650
You should have your breakfast, Son.

75
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:41,420
Make you feel better.

76
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:43,160
Protein, vitamins.

77
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:44,880
She said she'll call back?

78
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:47,670
Yes, she did.

79
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:49,230
Good morning, everyone!

80
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:52,540
Happy Turkey Day!

81
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:53,740
What's wrong?

82
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:58,970
Nothing. Absolutely nothing.

83
00:04:58,970 --> 00:05:01,070
What's gotten into him?

84
00:05:01,070 --> 00:05:03,140
He missed a phone call.

85
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,140
From ...?

86
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:07,990
Yes, Alexandra.

87
00:05:07,990 --> 00:05:13,270
It's nice to see young love.... Oh, to be young again!

88
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:16,270
Where's the coffee?
